    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c089b325_65c435e0",
        "filename": "fw-update/update_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002771
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-03T14:13:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair point — you\u0027re right that OR-then-worst can force AC on a device\nthat also advertises SelfContained. Reading DSP0267 v1.3.0 Table 5\nagain, multiple bits mean the component supports multiple methods and\nthe UA gets to pick. So for patchset 3 I\u0027ll switch to:\n\n  - per device: pick the lightest bit set as that device\u0027s effective\n    activation method\n  - package level: take the worst among those per-device picks\n\nAn \"AC + SelfContained\" device then correctly reduces to SelfContained,\nand we only land in Staged if at least one device is genuinely stuck\nat MediumReset / Reboot / DC / AC. Same change also removes the dead\nSelfContained / Automatic branches Vishnu flagged.\n\nDoes that match how you\u0027d read it, or would you pick a different\nper-device rule?",
      "parentUuid": "fe2f3061_66dbaea1",
      "revId": "ac31eb4e8a8e513d06d50a7c158733cb37e5ea40",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
