      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T10:17:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We currently don\u0027t publish any event saying that there the updated versions are active. Any successful update after this update would leave a stale event implying a manual activation is still required",
      "revId": "ac31eb4e8a8e513d06d50a7c158733cb37e5ea40",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec90bdd3_feb7ca98",
        "filename": "fw-update/update_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 453,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002771
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-03T14:13:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed — the awaiting-activation event needs a matching completion\nevent, otherwise consumers see a stale \"awaiting\" state after the\nnext update.\n\nThree options I\u0027m weighing for patchset 3:\n\n  (a) Add OpenBMC.0.1.FirmwareUpdateActivationComplete to the same\n      openbmc registry (paired with AwaitingActivation) and emit on\n      Staged→Active\n  (b) Reuse an existing DMTF Update event (e.g. UpdateSuccessful) at\n      the transition\n  (c) Mark the original phosphor-logging entry Resolved on transition\n\nLeaning toward (a) for symmetry and precise semantics. Any preference?",
      "parentUuid": "cffd35d4_2be03940",
      "revId": "ac31eb4e8a8e513d06d50a7c158733cb37e5ea40",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
